1
00:01:27,912 --> 00:01:33,785
SOBA RESTAURANT REBRAND!

2
00:01:39,958 --> 00:01:42,927
It's so cold! Want to have some warm soba?

3
00:01:43,127 --> 00:01:43,962
Sounds good!

4
00:01:46,965 --> 00:01:50,068
This restaurant didn't use to be popular at all.

5
00:01:52,637 --> 00:01:53,705
Thank you!

6
00:01:55,173 --> 00:01:56,407
I guess we can go in soon.

7
00:01:59,410 --> 00:02:01,479
You idiot! That's dangerous!

8
00:02:02,547 --> 00:02:03,348
Hey!

9
00:02:03,581 --> 00:02:04,716
-Ryotsu! -Ah?

10
00:02:09,487 --> 00:02:10,488
&lt;i&gt;This guy...&lt;/i&gt;

11
00:02:10,722 --> 00:02:13,558
&lt;i&gt;He's been appearing on TV and in magazines a lot lately.&lt;/i&gt;

12
00:02:13,758 --> 00:02:17,295
&lt;i&gt;Chogoro Ohmaeda, a gourmet critic.&lt;/i&gt;

13
00:02:18,296 --> 00:02:20,732
&lt;i&gt;This flavor is something else!&lt;/i&gt;

14
00:02:21,132 --> 00:02:24,369
Hmm, the restaurant's entrance is still something else.

15
00:02:24,602 --> 00:02:25,670
Is the owner here?

16
00:02:25,904 --> 00:02:27,772
Yes, yes. I'm coming!

17
00:02:28,206 --> 00:02:30,675
Oh, Ohmaeda-sensei. Please come in.

18
00:02:32,443 --> 00:02:34,112
You just cut in, you jerk!

19
00:02:34,312 --> 00:02:35,380
Easy, Ryotsu!

20
00:02:36,648 --> 00:02:37,782
Here you are.

21
00:02:37,982 --> 00:02:40,385
Hmm, the efficiency is something else.

22
00:02:45,390 --> 00:02:46,457
How snobby!

23
00:02:46,658 --> 00:02:49,527
We've been waiting for three hours in the cold.

24
00:03:15,053 --> 00:03:17,255
Hmm, this soba is something else!

25
00:03:17,488 --> 00:03:19,524
Th-Thank you very much!

26
00:03:19,991 --> 00:03:22,994
Ohmaeda-sensei's classic line, "It's something else"!

27
00:03:23,361 --> 00:03:26,497
As I expected, the soba here is first-rate.

28
00:03:26,698 --> 00:03:31,336
I don't care if it's something else, leave your seat once you're done eating!

29
00:03:32,103 --> 00:03:36,507
Owner, I want my acquaintances to taste this "something else" soba too.

30
00:03:36,708 --> 00:03:39,210
Please prepare 200 servings.

31
00:03:40,078 --> 00:03:43,848
It'll cost over 100,000 yen for 200 servings.

32
00:03:44,048 --> 00:03:49,587
Owner, I'm Chogoro Ohmaeda, Japan's number one gourmet critic!

33
00:03:50,455 --> 00:03:54,292
Of course, there's no charge! Please enjoy the meal with everyone.

34
00:03:57,395 --> 00:03:59,430
Keep up the good work.

35
00:03:59,664 --> 00:04:01,065
Thank you very much!

36
00:04:02,767 --> 00:04:04,235
Hmph, he's finally gone.

37
00:04:04,435 --> 00:04:06,437
Now it's our turn.

38
00:04:06,671 --> 00:04:07,572
"CLOSED TODAY"

39
00:04:07,772 --> 00:04:08,840
W-What?

40
00:04:09,407 --> 00:04:11,743
Hey, what do you mean by "closed"?

41
00:04:11,943 --> 00:04:17,315
We've waited three hours in the cold just for some warm soba!

42
00:04:17,548 --> 00:04:20,685
Ohmaeda-sensei took all the soba.

43
00:04:20,885 --> 00:04:23,488
What? Oh no...

44
00:04:23,721 --> 00:04:25,723
I'm the one who wants to cry.

45
00:04:26,324 --> 00:04:30,762
I wish I'd never been featured in this magazine. Damn it!

46
00:04:33,164 --> 00:04:37,735
So customers suddenly came because it was in this magazine.

47
00:04:38,403 --> 00:04:41,039
He's taking advantage of it and eating for free.

48
00:04:41,239 --> 00:04:42,473
What an outrageous guy!

49
00:04:44,976 --> 00:04:48,112
Jeez, I don't care anymore if it tastes a little bad.

50
00:04:48,312 --> 00:04:51,082
Is there any place that serves warm soba?

51
00:04:51,883 --> 00:04:54,252
Ryotsu, how about here?

52
00:04:54,452 --> 00:04:55,320
What?

53
00:04:56,754 --> 00:04:57,588
Excuse us.

54
00:05:01,759 --> 00:05:04,762
There's no sign of any customers.

55
00:05:05,363 --> 00:05:06,664
It's dangerous. Let's go.

56
00:05:06,898 --> 00:05:08,266
Huh, why?

57
00:05:08,466 --> 00:05:12,070
Don't you get it? A place with so few customers isn't normal.

58
00:05:12,270 --> 00:05:16,207
I bet the soba's so bad, you'll never want it again.

59
00:05:21,546 --> 00:05:22,914
Are you customers?

60
00:05:23,114 --> 00:05:25,083
Well, that was our intention, but...

61
00:05:25,283 --> 00:05:26,684
Thank you very much!

62
00:05:26,918 --> 00:05:28,319
What's wrong?

63
00:05:28,519 --> 00:05:31,356
You're actually the fifth customers here.

64
00:05:31,556 --> 00:05:34,826
The fifth customers today, huh? Yeah, looks like it.

65
00:05:35,026 --> 00:05:37,362
No, the fifth customers since I opened the place.

66
00:05:37,562 --> 00:05:38,629
What?

67
00:05:38,830 --> 00:05:40,331
Oh, wait!

68
00:05:40,531 --> 00:05:41,632
When did you open?

69
00:05:41,833 --> 00:05:42,767
Three years ago.

70
00:05:42,967 --> 00:05:44,402
Th-Three years ago?

71
00:05:46,371 --> 00:05:48,873
I'll make soba right away. What would you like?

72
00:05:49,107 --> 00:05:52,677
Oh, actually, I suddenly got a stomachache...

73
00:05:52,877 --> 00:05:53,878
No way...

74
00:05:54,512 --> 00:05:57,415
Ryotsu, I feel sorry for him. Let's eat here.

75
00:05:57,648 --> 00:06:01,686
What if the soba here really makes our stomachs go bad?

76
00:06:01,886 --> 00:06:05,823
If anything happens, the Nakagawa Corporation's medical team will handle it.

77
00:06:06,023 --> 00:06:06,891
Well...

78
00:06:09,127 --> 00:06:11,229
Let's be his fifth customers.

79
00:06:11,429 --> 00:06:12,697
Please.

80
00:06:12,897 --> 00:06:16,567
Okay, we'll be the fifth victims then.

81
00:06:25,176 --> 00:06:26,844
Thank you for waiting.

82
00:06:27,378 --> 00:06:32,049
The soba looks awful. Let's eat it quickly and go back to the station.

83
00:06:36,287 --> 00:06:37,255
Stop watching!

84
00:06:37,455 --> 00:06:38,689
S-Sorry!

85
00:06:38,890 --> 00:06:41,058
Curious about our reaction, right?

86
00:06:41,259 --> 00:06:42,260
Y-Yes.

87
00:06:42,460 --> 00:06:47,031
I'll tell you what I think after I've finished. Wait over there till then.

88
00:06:47,231 --> 00:06:48,399
Oh, sure.

89
00:06:52,370 --> 00:06:56,774
Hmm, it's just ordinary soba, not so bad that I can't eat it.

90
00:06:59,911 --> 00:07:01,746
Oh, this is...!

91
00:07:01,946 --> 00:07:03,314
What's the matter, Nakagawa?

92
00:07:03,548 --> 00:07:05,283
Owner, I'd like to ask you something.

93
00:07:05,483 --> 00:07:07,018
Yes, what is it?

94
00:07:07,618 --> 00:07:11,455
Could it be that this soba uses buckwheat flour from Yamada Farm?

95
00:07:11,656 --> 00:07:12,957
Yes, that's right.

96
00:07:13,191 --> 00:07:15,726
What's Yamada Farm?

97
00:07:16,194 --> 00:07:21,432
It's the farm of Dengoro Yamada, a renowned buckwheat flour master.

98
00:07:24,235 --> 00:07:29,040
His buckwheat flour is said to be the best in Japan, but it's hard to get.

99
00:07:29,240 --> 00:07:34,412
It's only used in a few restaurants in Nakagawa Corporation's culinary division.

100
00:07:34,612 --> 00:07:40,051
I've been close with him for years, so I can get it at a lower price.

101
00:07:40,418 --> 00:07:41,652
I knew it!

102
00:07:41,886 --> 00:07:46,991
And the soy sauce used in the soup stock is made at Sato Brewery, isn't it?

103
00:07:47,225 --> 00:07:48,059
R-Right.

104
00:07:48,659 --> 00:07:52,463
Sato Brewery has been making soy sauce by hand since the early 1800s,

105
00:07:52,663 --> 00:07:56,801
conveying the traditional taste of Kishu, said to be the birthplace of soy sauce.

106
00:07:57,001 --> 00:08:00,972
It's considered to be the finest of all soy sauces.

107
00:08:01,339 --> 00:08:05,309
But that's not all. The sliced dried bonito and kelp

108
00:08:05,509 --> 00:08:08,980
are also definitely first-class, producing this rich soup stock.

109
00:08:09,180 --> 00:08:13,117
Even the green onions are firm and shiny, and of excellent quality.

110
00:08:13,317 --> 00:08:17,788
And the blend of seven spices creates an exquisite harmony of flavors.

111
00:08:18,389 --> 00:08:23,294
The spiciness is perfect, and it's clearly made with carefully selected ingredients.

112
00:08:23,661 --> 00:08:28,266
How can you use such amazing ingredients and make such ordinary soba?

113
00:08:28,699 --> 00:08:31,969
Ordinary? Look at your bowl.

114
00:08:33,137 --> 00:08:34,472
Ah, when did I...

115
00:08:34,672 --> 00:08:37,675
That's what truly delicious food is like.

116
00:08:37,875 --> 00:08:40,478
It gets into your body naturally.

117
00:08:42,013 --> 00:08:44,148
Owner, give me another bowlful.

118
00:08:44,348 --> 00:08:44,982
S-Sure!

119
00:08:47,885 --> 00:08:51,322
It sure is pretty good if you taste it carefully.

120
00:08:51,522 --> 00:08:52,356
Right?

121
00:08:52,556 --> 00:08:55,693
It has such good flavor. You should advertise it more.

122
00:08:55,893 --> 00:08:58,129
I'm not really good at showy things.

123
00:08:58,329 --> 00:09:00,064
Even so, it seems strange.

124
00:09:00,298 --> 00:09:03,534
If it tastes this good, customers should come by word of mouth.

125
00:09:03,734 --> 00:09:06,771
There's a deeper reason why no customers are coming.

126
00:09:07,004 --> 00:09:07,838
A deeper reason?

127
00:09:08,439 --> 00:09:10,608
I'll never forget three years ago...

128
00:09:11,776 --> 00:09:16,414
&lt;i&gt;on a day when light snow was falling, this restaurant opened.&lt;/i&gt;

129
00:09:17,248 --> 00:09:19,550
"OPEN TODAY"

130
00:09:19,750 --> 00:09:23,154
&lt;i&gt;I was nervously waiting for the first customer to arrive.&lt;/i&gt;

131
00:09:23,354 --> 00:09:24,388
&lt;i&gt;And then...&lt;/i&gt;

132
00:09:26,157 --> 00:09:26,991
Excuse me.

133
00:09:30,328 --> 00:09:32,096
What? Ohmaeda?

134
00:09:32,463 --> 00:09:35,099
Did Ohmaeda-sensei come all the way here just to eat?

135
00:09:35,533 --> 00:09:37,902
No, he just wanted to use the restroom.

136
00:09:40,171 --> 00:09:42,940
Hmm, so this is a soba restaurant.

137
00:09:43,174 --> 00:09:45,810
It's too ordinary to notice,

138
00:09:46,043 --> 00:09:48,346
but just as well, I'll eat lunch here.

139
00:09:48,879 --> 00:09:51,048
Yes, I'll make it right away.

140
00:09:51,916 --> 00:09:56,721
&lt;i&gt;Since he was my first customer, I put all my skills into making it.&lt;/i&gt;

141
00:09:56,921 --> 00:09:57,922
Here you are.

142
00:09:58,389 --> 00:09:59,223
Hmm...

143
00:10:21,245 --> 00:10:23,147
How was it, sir?

144
00:10:23,581 --> 00:10:26,150
It's just ordinary. It tastes nothing special.

145
00:10:26,384 --> 00:10:27,651
I see...

146
00:10:31,155 --> 00:10:34,225
Well, it'll be 700 yen.

147
00:10:35,760 --> 00:10:40,398
Owner, you don't know who I am, do you?

148
00:10:40,598 --> 00:10:44,468
I'm Chogoro Ohmaeda, the gourmet critic.

149
00:10:44,669 --> 00:10:48,472
Yes, so, a bowl of kake-soba will be 700 yen.

150
00:10:48,672 --> 00:10:52,977
I'm Chogoro Ohmaeda, Japan's number one gourmet critic!

151
00:10:53,177 --> 00:10:56,180
So, a bowl of kake-soba will be 700 yen.

152
00:10:56,414 --> 00:10:59,150
I said I'm Ohmaeda!

153
00:10:59,784 --> 00:11:02,319
So, it'll be 700 yen...

154
00:11:02,520 --> 00:11:04,622
So, I'm Ohmaeda!

155
00:11:05,122 --> 00:11:06,624
It'll be 700 yen...

156
00:11:07,258 --> 00:11:10,628
Unfortunately, I don't carry cash.

157
00:11:11,128 --> 00:11:12,997
Will this be enough?

158
00:11:13,197 --> 00:11:16,734
It's pure gold, worth around 20,000 to 30,000 yen.

159
00:11:16,967 --> 00:11:19,303
Th-Thank you very much.

160
00:11:21,105 --> 00:11:23,007
Owner, what's the name of this restaurant?

161
00:11:23,207 --> 00:11:25,509
It's "Tanaka Soba."

162
00:11:25,710 --> 00:11:27,712
"Tanaka Soba."

163
00:11:28,646 --> 00:11:30,381
I'll remember that.

164
00:11:34,552 --> 00:11:38,055
&lt;i&gt;In the end, that fountain pen was a blatant fake.&lt;/i&gt;

165
00:11:38,289 --> 00:11:39,390
What a stingy guy!

166
00:11:39,590 --> 00:11:41,992
&lt;i&gt;I was shocked a week later.&lt;/i&gt;

167
00:11:42,193 --> 00:11:45,830
&lt;i&gt;He had completely insulted my restaurant in a magazine.&lt;/i&gt;

168
00:11:46,997 --> 00:11:49,200
"It's not something that humans should eat."

169
00:11:49,400 --> 00:11:51,836
"Even if the public forgives it, I don't."

170
00:11:52,036 --> 00:11:53,504
"Minus seven stars."

171
00:11:53,704 --> 00:11:56,407
-That's terrible. -Don't display such an article!

172
00:11:56,607 --> 00:11:59,543
But since my restaurant was featured...

173
00:11:59,743 --> 00:12:02,046
It'll only give a bad impression!

174
00:12:02,246 --> 00:12:06,517
Still, it's a terrible article, full of completely misguided criticism.

175
00:12:06,917 --> 00:12:08,786
Must be revenge for not eating free!

176
00:12:09,220 --> 00:12:12,590
I can't forgive him for taking the soba I was supposed to eat.

177
00:12:12,790 --> 00:12:15,960
And he gave such delicious soba a minus seven-star rating!

178
00:12:16,193 --> 00:12:20,765
It's outrageous that someone with no taste calls himself a gourmet critic!

179
00:12:20,965 --> 00:12:24,535
All right, I'll show him what happens when he makes me angry!

180
00:12:24,735 --> 00:12:25,569
Okay, owner?

181
00:12:25,769 --> 00:12:27,738
Yes, if you can.

182
00:12:28,105 --> 00:12:30,274
Leave it to me. I have a good idea.

183
00:12:30,508 --> 00:12:33,744
I'll make you pay for this, Chogoro Ohmaeda!

184
00:12:35,946 --> 00:12:37,782
"TANAKA SOBA"

185
00:12:37,982 --> 00:12:39,350
"CLOSED"

186
00:12:39,717 --> 00:12:43,454
To bring Ohmaeda down, some sacrifices are necessary.

187
00:12:43,654 --> 00:12:45,089
Are you ready for that?

188
00:12:45,289 --> 00:12:45,956
Y-Yes.

189
00:12:46,190 --> 00:12:50,294
Now, let's start "the operation to take Chogoro Ohmaeda down."

190
00:12:57,835 --> 00:12:58,903
W-What are you doing!

191
00:12:59,103 --> 00:13:02,373
To impress a gourmet critic, such an ordinary appearance won't do!

192
00:13:02,573 --> 00:13:04,475
It needs tradition and prestige!

193
00:13:05,009 --> 00:13:09,313
I see! So you're going for a look that says it's weathered the years.

194
00:13:09,547 --> 00:13:10,848
That's right.

195
00:13:21,158 --> 00:13:24,161
Such ordinary bowls won't do, either!

196
00:13:25,963 --> 00:13:28,766
M-My restaurant...

197
00:13:30,334 --> 00:13:32,336
Ryotsu, is there anything I can do?

198
00:13:32,570 --> 00:13:36,707
Yes! Bring anything traditional and prestigious!

199
00:13:37,508 --> 00:13:38,576
Roger!

200
00:13:40,411 --> 00:13:41,512
Next...

201
00:13:48,419 --> 00:13:50,454
Ryo-san! What are you doing?

202
00:13:50,855 --> 00:13:51,956
Oh, good timing!

203
00:13:52,489 --> 00:13:56,460
You guys said you made bowls in art class at school, right?

204
00:13:56,660 --> 00:13:59,697
Yes, but they're dusty and cracked.

205
00:13:59,897 --> 00:14:01,332
That's even better.

206
00:14:01,532 --> 00:14:04,134
Bring them here. Borrow some from your friends, too.

207
00:14:04,335 --> 00:14:05,970
Okay, Ryo-san!

208
00:14:09,874 --> 00:14:11,542
"NAL NAKAGAWA CORPORATION"

209
00:14:12,076 --> 00:14:13,477
Oh, here they come.

210
00:14:35,900 --> 00:14:38,369
I borrowed them from museums around the world.

211
00:14:38,569 --> 00:14:40,938
They all tell the story of human history.

212
00:14:41,171 --> 00:14:41,872
Very good.

213
00:14:42,072 --> 00:14:46,176
Well, it seems strange to me that these things are in a soba restaurant.

214
00:14:46,377 --> 00:14:48,479
That's okay. It's better to bluff like this.

215
00:14:49,113 --> 00:14:52,583
Oh, let's say this is an opening gift from Cleopatra.

216
00:14:52,783 --> 00:14:56,186
"CONGRATULATIONS ON YOUR GRAND OPENING FROM CLEOPATRA"

217
00:14:56,387 --> 00:14:57,688
That's crazy!

218
00:14:58,188 --> 00:15:00,524
It should be like this...

219
00:15:02,226 --> 00:15:04,395
I'll break one of the pillars, too.

220
00:15:04,595 --> 00:15:08,265
Stop! If you cut this, the whole building will collapse!

221
00:15:08,499 --> 00:15:09,400
Oh, I see.

222
00:15:09,600 --> 00:15:12,036
-Ryo-san! -We brought them!

223
00:15:16,073 --> 00:15:17,708
All right, good job.

224
00:15:18,242 --> 00:15:19,910
So, the restaurant is ready.

225
00:15:20,811 --> 00:15:22,146
Next...

226
00:15:22,579 --> 00:15:23,814
N-No way...

227
00:15:24,048 --> 00:15:26,684
Oh, no! Please don't do that!

228
00:15:26,884 --> 00:15:29,620
To impress a gourmet critic, you must be a unique owner.

229
00:15:29,820 --> 00:15:31,755
No, that's too far! Stop!

230
00:15:31,955 --> 00:15:33,757
Don't make that creepy voice!

231
00:15:38,262 --> 00:15:39,897
Huh? That bike...

232
00:15:42,433 --> 00:15:44,401
You're slacking off again, Kankichi!

233
00:15:44,601 --> 00:15:45,135
Hi!

234
00:15:45,369 --> 00:15:46,637
Nakagawa-san!

235
00:15:47,104 --> 00:15:48,973
It's done. Come on.

236
00:15:49,173 --> 00:15:49,907
B-But...

237
00:15:50,107 --> 00:15:51,308
Don't be shy!

238
00:15:51,909 --> 00:15:53,377
You're slacking again!

239
00:15:53,577 --> 00:15:55,079
I'll tell Chief Ohara.

240
00:15:55,279 --> 00:15:56,013
Hey!

241
00:15:56,246 --> 00:15:57,014
Ta-da!

242
00:16:07,991 --> 00:16:09,560
Pervert!

243
00:16:09,760 --> 00:16:13,130
Pervert? Did they mean me...?

244
00:16:15,733 --> 00:16:17,634
Look, he's so happy.

245
00:16:17,835 --> 00:16:20,037
He's lamenting his misfortune.

246
00:16:20,270 --> 00:16:21,839
The stage is set!

247
00:16:22,039 --> 00:16:24,341
-Nakagawa, round up some fake customers. -Got it.

248
00:16:24,842 --> 00:16:26,844
All that's left is to corner the prey!

249
00:16:35,319 --> 00:16:39,356
Are you sure there's a soba restaurant out here that's worth lining up for?

250
00:16:39,590 --> 00:16:44,795
Yes. viewers say the line stretches about two kilometers every day.

251
00:16:44,995 --> 00:16:46,163
Oh, is that it?

252
00:16:50,167 --> 00:16:52,369
This is amazing!

253
00:16:52,603 --> 00:16:56,006
Are all these people lining up for the soba restaurant?

254
00:17:12,456 --> 00:17:15,225
"SPECIAL REPORT: THE LEGENDARY SOBA RESTAURANT EXISTS!"

255
00:17:15,626 --> 00:17:20,164
Today, together with Chogoro Ohmaeda. Japan's number one gourmet critic,

256
00:17:20,364 --> 00:17:22,566
I'll visit this legendary soba restaurant.

257
00:17:22,800 --> 00:17:25,469
I'm Chogoro Ohmaeda!

258
00:17:25,669 --> 00:17:27,071
Ohmaeda-sensei!

259
00:17:27,271 --> 00:17:28,539
Who are you?

260
00:17:28,739 --> 00:17:34,211
We heard that you'll be visiting this restaurant. May we join you?

261
00:17:34,411 --> 00:17:36,547
Yes, but don't disturb us.

262
00:17:38,282 --> 00:17:42,886
Ohmaeda-sensei, what's your first impression of the restaurant?

263
00:17:45,055 --> 00:17:49,593
Hey, this place has been around since 825, passed down for 20 generations.

264
00:17:49,827 --> 00:17:53,430
There's talk of designating it an Important Cultural Property of Japan.

265
00:17:53,964 --> 00:17:56,400
&lt;i&gt;An Important Cultural Property!&lt;/i&gt;

266
00:17:56,767 --> 00:17:58,569
"IMPORTANT CULTURAL PROPERTY"

267
00:17:59,236 --> 00:18:03,040
This restaurant has probably been in business since around the early 800s.

268
00:18:03,941 --> 00:18:05,909
Look at this mark.

269
00:18:06,109 --> 00:18:11,448
It must be the remnants of a fierce battle during the Meiji Restoration.

270
00:18:11,682 --> 00:18:13,417
That was made by Ryotsu.

271
00:18:13,617 --> 00:18:15,953
It's surprisingly easy to fool him.

272
00:18:16,153 --> 00:18:21,058
This casually placed mummy is a masterpiece that evokes a long history.

273
00:18:22,092 --> 00:18:24,294
This restaurant is something else!

274
00:18:27,564 --> 00:18:31,468
"Something else" has already come out! This looks promising!

275
00:18:32,536 --> 00:18:33,070
Excuse us...

276
00:18:33,270 --> 00:18:35,072
Get out, you idiot!

277
00:18:37,274 --> 00:18:41,979
You're only allowed to use chili once here, but you used it twice!

278
00:18:42,179 --> 00:18:44,748
Owner, tell him off good and proper!

279
00:18:49,019 --> 00:18:51,154
What are you doing? Hurry up!

280
00:18:51,355 --> 00:18:53,357
Am I really going out like this?

281
00:18:53,590 --> 00:18:56,493
Of course! Make up your mind already!

282
00:18:56,994 --> 00:19:02,299
Because of what he wrote, you've only had five customers in three years.

283
00:19:02,499 --> 00:19:04,468
Remember that!

284
00:19:08,672 --> 00:19:09,373
Go!

285
00:19:12,176 --> 00:19:13,644
I'm sorry, owner...

286
00:19:20,017 --> 00:19:23,353
Anyone who doesn't follow the rules of the restaurant ain't welcome!

287
00:19:23,587 --> 00:19:24,855
Don't ever come back!

288
00:19:25,055 --> 00:19:27,658
Amazing! He has a craftsman's spirit!

289
00:19:27,858 --> 00:19:29,526
What do you think, Ohmaeda-sensei?

290
00:19:30,294 --> 00:19:33,830
Just like that, he kicked someone from the British royal family, too.

291
00:19:34,031 --> 00:19:36,333
Yeah. But they loved him for it.

292
00:19:36,533 --> 00:19:39,536
Now his soba gets flown to Buckingham Palace every week!

293
00:19:39,770 --> 00:19:41,705
&lt;i&gt;The British royal family!&lt;/i&gt;

294
00:19:41,939 --> 00:19:43,807
"BRITISH ROYAL FAMILY"

295
00:19:45,008 --> 00:19:50,347
His determination to preserve the taste of soba, and the owner's appearance!

296
00:19:50,547 --> 00:19:52,049
He wears traditional geta,

297
00:19:52,249 --> 00:19:56,019
but isn't content with tradition and actively incorporates Western styles.

298
00:19:56,220 --> 00:20:00,324
He embodies the ideas of "learning from the past" and "fusion of East and West"!

299
00:20:00,524 --> 00:20:03,427
The owner is something else!

300
00:20:05,028 --> 00:20:06,863
"Something else" again!

301
00:20:07,064 --> 00:20:08,632
Who are you guys?

302
00:20:09,032 --> 00:20:12,836
Don't you know me? I'm Chogoro Ohmaeda, a gourmet critic.

303
00:20:13,036 --> 00:20:14,671
We came here for a TV interview.

304
00:20:14,871 --> 00:20:16,873
What? TV?

305
00:20:17,207 --> 00:20:19,543
You idiot! No interviews here!

306
00:20:19,743 --> 00:20:24,881
Put it on TV, and people who can't even taste real soba will flood in.

307
00:20:25,082 --> 00:20:27,985
If we get any more customers, we'll be too busy to handle it!

308
00:20:28,185 --> 00:20:29,353
Hey, don't show us!

309
00:20:29,553 --> 00:20:32,656
A customer is a customer! We'll just serve soba as usual!

310
00:20:33,357 --> 00:20:35,192
Yes, you're absolutely right.

311
00:20:37,594 --> 00:20:38,729
Wonderful!

312
00:20:39,229 --> 00:20:44,101
I've had all kinds of food around the world, but never had soba this good!

313
00:20:44,534 --> 00:20:46,603
I'll put the money here!

314
00:20:49,706 --> 00:20:53,910
No wonder the Secretary-General of the U.N. is a regular customer.

315
00:20:54,111 --> 00:20:57,581
Anyone who says it's not good is not human.

316
00:20:58,015 --> 00:21:00,317
&lt;i&gt;The U.N. Secretary-General...&lt;/i&gt;

317
00:21:00,550 --> 00:21:02,319
"U.N. SECRETARY-GENERAL"

318
00:21:09,426 --> 00:21:10,394
Thanks for waiting.

319
00:21:11,094 --> 00:21:13,897
Now, what about the taste of the soba?

320
00:21:35,786 --> 00:21:41,758
Perfect soba, bold broth, fine-cut green onions, and this artistic bowl!

321
00:21:41,958 --> 00:21:43,260
I made it!

322
00:21:43,460 --> 00:21:45,829
All of them are first-class!

323
00:21:46,330 --> 00:21:47,998
They are something else.

324
00:21:48,198 --> 00:21:53,904
As proof that this restaurant is truly something else, I award it seven stars!

325
00:22:00,277 --> 00:22:02,179
Oh, you must be happy, too.

326
00:22:02,379 --> 00:22:03,680
Hey, Ohmaeda!

327
00:22:05,282 --> 00:22:06,550
What happened?

328
00:22:07,017 --> 00:22:08,852
What are you doing? How rude!

329
00:22:09,086 --> 00:22:11,555
Shut up! Look at this!

330
00:22:13,523 --> 00:22:15,492
"Tanaka Soba"?

331
00:22:16,093 --> 00:22:18,762
Does this finally jog your memory?

332
00:22:20,764 --> 00:22:23,200
-Ah, this restaurant is... -Finally, you remember.

333
00:22:23,400 --> 00:22:28,138
Yes, it's "Tanaka Soba" which you gave minus seven stars three years ago!

334
00:22:28,505 --> 00:22:32,309
-Hey, what's going on? -What does it mean?

335
00:22:32,509 --> 00:22:36,513
This restaurant hasn't changed how it makes soba since three years ago.

336
00:22:36,713 --> 00:22:40,484
It's always served the best soba with the finest ingredients!

337
00:22:40,884 --> 00:22:42,652
I didn't realize that.

338
00:22:44,688 --> 00:22:48,558
Now you confessed that you don't know what soba tastes like!

339
00:22:49,693 --> 00:22:51,061
Oh, shoot...!

340
00:22:51,261 --> 00:22:54,564
You're no gourmet critic.

341
00:22:54,798 --> 00:22:56,566
Just a damn fool with no taste!

342
00:22:59,336 --> 00:23:00,537
What does it mean?

343
00:23:00,737 --> 00:23:02,406
Is what he said true?

344
00:23:02,606 --> 00:23:03,974
Please explain!

345
00:23:04,841 --> 00:23:06,543
N-No comment!

346
00:23:10,447 --> 00:23:12,282
Our operation nailed it!

347
00:23:12,616 --> 00:23:16,820
The legendary soba restaurant existed, but Ohmaeda-sensei was a tasteless fraud!

348
00:23:19,689 --> 00:23:22,426
"Tanaka Soba" seems to be doing well since then.

349
00:23:22,893 --> 00:23:23,860
Yeah.

350
00:23:24,060 --> 00:23:27,931
But after that, I haven't heard anything about Ohmaeda-sensei.

351
00:23:28,465 --> 00:23:29,399
Huh?!

352
00:23:29,599 --> 00:23:30,434
What's up?

353
00:23:31,201 --> 00:23:34,004
"A mysterious home cooking critic appears!"

354
00:23:34,204 --> 00:23:37,407
"Recently, a self-proclaimed home cooking critic showed up in Tokyo."

355
00:23:37,607 --> 00:23:41,178
"He goes into people's homes and eats meals with them."

356
00:23:41,378 --> 00:23:42,946
This is Ohmaeda-sensei, isn't it?

357
00:23:43,180 --> 00:23:46,950
Good grief! This guy is something else.

358
00:23:49,486 --> 00:23:51,621
&lt;i&gt;I'm something else.&lt;/i&gt;

359
00:23:53,323 --> 00:23:57,227
TODAY'S DAMAGE REPORT

360
00:23:57,427 --> 00:24:01,331
ZERO
